# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI Asset Governance Tool — root configuration
#
# This is the single source of truth for both `docker compose` and the setup /
# start scripts. `scripts/setup.sh` creates `.env` from this file on first run
# and fills in random secrets. For a local (non-Docker) backend run the script
# also derives `backend/.env` from these values; `backend/.env` may be edited
# to override anything here for backend-only workflows.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# How the database is provided:
#   managed  – the app starts a bundled PostgreSQL (no Docker, no system install)
#   docker   – the postgres service in docker-compose.yml
#   url      – you point DATABASE_URL at an existing PostgreSQL
DB_MODE=docker

# PostgreSQL credentials (used by the docker `postgres` service and to build
# DATABASE_URL). setup.sh generates a random POSTGRES_PASSWORD on first run.
POSTGRES_USER=aibom
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
POSTGRES_DB=aibom

# Full connection string. Leave blank to let the scripts build it from the parts
# above (host 127.0.0.1:55432 for local/docker, or the compose-internal host in
# the container). Set it explicitly when DB_MODE=url.
DATABASE_URL=

# Required. setup.sh generates a strong value (openssl rand -hex 32).
JWT_SECRET=

# Ports. All three are free to change — setup.sh / setup.ps1 prompt for them and
# thread them through docker-compose, the scripts, and the Vite dev server.
#   PORT          – the API and (when SERVE_STATIC is on) the web app
#   DB_PORT       – PostgreSQL on the host (managed + docker database modes)
#   FRONTEND_PORT – the Vite dev server, used only by `--mode=local` + start.sh
PORT=4000
DB_PORT=55432
FRONTEND_PORT=5173

# Address published ports bind to on the host. 127.0.0.1 keeps the app
# reachable only from this machine; set 0.0.0.0 to expose it on the network
# (put a TLS-terminating reverse proxy in front — see docs/deployment.md).
BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1

# Public URL the app is reached at (used for links in notifications, etc.).
APP_URL=http://localhost:4000

# Only needed when the SPA is served from a different origin than the API.
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:4000

# Set when running behind a reverse proxy: "1" for one hop, or a trusted subnet.
# TRUST_PROXY=1

# Log verbosity: fatal | error | warn | info | debug | trace
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Evidence-file uploads. Files land under ATTACHMENTS_DIR (default: data/attachments
# — gitignored; mount a volume in Docker to persist). ATTACHMENTS_MAX_MB caps a
# single upload.
# ATTACHMENTS_DIR=data/attachments
# ATTACHMENTS_MAX_MB=10

# Serves Swagger UI + the OpenAPI document at /api/docs. Defaults to on outside
# production; set explicitly to opt in (or out) in production.
# ENABLE_API_DOCS=true

# Initial admin account (seed time only — read by prisma:seed:reference).
# setup.sh prompts for these; a blank ADMIN_PASSWORD generates a random one.
# ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
# ADMIN_NAME=Admin User
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=
